{"title":"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The number of points common to the graphs of\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/8/d58740c43826e95a0465cd02c9b1e9e9219bb1a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-y+2)(3x+y-4)=0 \\text{    and     } (x+y-2)(2x-5y+7)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"481\" height=\"18\" />\nis:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/52139eba22203c4cbeeb28c71ced130f32921063.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) } 2\\quad \\text{(B) } 4\\quad \\text{(C) } 6\\quad \\text{(D) } 16\\quad \\text{(E) } \\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"282\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Zero_Product_Property\" title=\"Zero Product Property\">Zero Product Property</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/8/b58dde5c69ebffab1344871b9f4bb57384655d5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-y+2=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"106\" height=\"16\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/3/e136ab10efa751b26c382543e988a7cffa814cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x+y-4=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"115\" height=\"16\" /> in the first equation and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/9/25999fe8ee4093af4a91942a4ea7e19709fb54a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y-2=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"106\" height=\"16\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/5/fe5dff89399d3c7d6ecd1aa0cb4d108d0d719e78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x-5y+7=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"124\" height=\"16\" /> in the second equation.  Thus, from the first equation, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/b/39bbdaf4f43870b9205628fbb11072a2a2ecd9d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = x+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/3/3937f795a909333e5f3a8080cf66fec8f29554f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y =-3x+4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"98\" height=\"16\" />, and from the second equation, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/6/c562b3bdc221e749cbc1037f0bdee9d2eea96ed4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=-x+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"89\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08defc65aef2d29f2715d5a4c5d1f64323b74514.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{2}{5}x + \\frac{7}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"91\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>If a point is common to the two graphs, then the point must be in one of the lines in the first equation as well as one of the lines in the second equation.  Since the slopes of the lines are different, none of the lines are parallel.  Thus, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/b/96bfa781745537f19408c574a0f66f44ee420270.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot 2 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"111\" height=\"28\" /> points of intersection in the two graphs.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME\" title=\"1969 AHSME\">1969 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1969 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1969\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1